# FTL Modula-2 (MD.COM/M2.COM) and ZMAC are line-oriented.  LF-only source
# collapses to a single line: MD.COM reports "ERROR 81 end of file reached
# before program complete", ZMAC reports "INPUT LINE TOO LONG".
#
# These files are copied byte for byte onto an SD card and read on the
# Zephyr-80 via SDGET, so the CRLF has to survive in the stored blob, not just
# in a checkout.  -text stops git normalizing them in either direction.
#
# The RunCPM builds are unaffected: copy_text() in TOOLS normalizes to LF and
# re-expands to CRLF while staging, so it is idempotent.

SRC/**   -text
TEST/**  -text
